  "_labelling": [
    "Labels are hand-checked against fixtures/cato. A chunk is labelled relevant only when its own",
    "text answers the query, not merely because its document does.",
    "Gong transcripts are chunked into six-turn windows that overlap by one turn, so several windows",
    "of one call can restate the same point. Labelling every overlapping window would make recall@5",
    "unreachable by construction, so each source document contributes at most one label per case: the",
    "single window that most directly answers the query. This is strict on the retriever, not lenient",
    "- returning a neighbouring window of the right call still scores as a miss.",
    "The retriever admits at most one policy chunk into its ranked selection, so no case labels two.",
    "forbiddenEvidenceIds are chunks the persona must never be handed for that query (a",
    "sensitive-pricing note without the grant, or a source family outside their authorized set).",
    "Any of them appearing anywhere in the returned evidence counts as permission leakage."
  ],
